 | M14 menus (part 1)   | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+4 tests in `menu.rs`, 1 in `touch_ui.rs`) | `menu.rs`: b1.7.3's `GuiMainMenu` (a rotating cube-map panorama, `render/panorama.rs`; `mclogo.png`, rotated splash; dirt on the other screens), `GuiSelectWorld` (scrolling list, double tap plays), `GuiCreateWorld` (name, seed, world type), delete confirm, "Loading level"; textures from the original jar (`tools/gen_menu.py`). Worlds live in `saves/<folder>/`; the pause menu got "Save and quit to title". The renderer button is gone (Vulkan first, GLES fallback stays automatic). See ROADMAP changelog. |
 | M14b Options + game menu | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+5 tests in `options.rs`, 1 in `touch_ui.rs`) | `options.rs`: b1.7.3's `GameSettings` (`options.txt`), `GuiOptions`, `GuiVideoSettings`, `GuiControls`, `GuiSlider` and `GuiIngameMenu`, from the pause button and the title screen's "Options...". Replaces the old pause menu (its Reset world button is gone); Pregen, Fly and LoD debug stay top-left; new `LoD: ON/OFF` button in Options. Sensitivity, invert, render distance, GUI scale, performance cap and difficulty act; music, sound, bobbing, anaglyph, advanced OpenGL, graphics, smooth lighting and the keys are stored only. See ROADMAP changelog. |
 | Options list (Sodium layout, 2026-11-01) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+9 tests in `options.rs`, +4 in `ui.rs`; `tools/optlist_proto.py` runs here: layout, text widths, tips and the clip maths against the real font); **NOT b1.7.3** | `options.rs` + new `ui.rs` + `menu.rs`: the options screen is Sodium's `VideoSettingsScreen` in b1.7.3's skin. ONE scrolling list of every setting (General, Graphics, Performance, Effects, Controls, Controller buttons, Controller tuning), each row its name on the left and a stone button or slider on the right; a page list down the left jumps to a section and lights the section in view as the list scrolls (LB / RB step it); group headings; a description pane (beside the list on a wide screen, a strip under it on a narrow one) explains the last tapped setting; settings that are saved but read by nothing (Graphics, Smooth Lighting, Advanced OpenGL, 3D Anaglyph, the keys) are dim, like Sodium's unavailable options. A drag scrolls (a drag that starts on a slider and goes along it moves the slider, one that goes up scrolls), a tap acts on lift. The Keys / Controller tabs and the Tuning... page are gone (one list), Dig Delay lives under Controls only. Without a scissor in the HUD pass, `ui::clip` cuts the quads at the list's edges. The same look (title with rules and studs, bevelled panels, coloured world-kind tags, empty-list hint, shared scroll bar) on the title screen, world list, create / rename / delete screens and the game menu. Not done: search, kinetic scrolling, a mouse wheel (no events for it), restyling the atmosphere editor. Controls (look and keys, pad buttons, pad tuning) is a tab of its own beside Settings; Graphics has an FOV slider (30 .. 110, 70 by default) and Brightness and Gamma percent sliders (50% .. 150%, final pass of both renderers). |
-| M15 Controller (Controllify port) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+7 tests in `gamepad.rs`, 1 in `options.rs`) | `input/gamepad.rs`: isXander's Controllify, the parts b1.7.3 has. Sticks walk and look (Controllify's deadzone, 6 look curves, 10 deg/tick at 100%), triggers dig / hit / place, bumpers and the hotbar wheel pick slots, a virtual mouse drives every menu and container, touch buttons hide while a pad is in use, rumble on damage / block break / explosion (`rumble.rs`, JNI). New **Controls > Controller** tab (buttons page + tuning page), saved as `pad_*` in `options.txt`. Not ported: gyro, DualSense extras, on-screen keyboard, glyph packs, chat / drop / perspective (not in mc-rs / b1.7.3); sprint is the row below, on L3. |
+| M15 Controller (Controllify port) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+7 tests in `gamepad.rs`, 1 in `options.rs`) | `input/gamepad.rs`: isXander's Controllify, the parts b1.7.3 has. Sticks walk and look (Controllify's deadzone, 6 look curves, 10 deg/tick at 100%), triggers dig / hit / place, bumpers and the hotbar wheel pick slots, a virtual mouse drives every menu and container, touch buttons hide while a pad is in use, rumble on damage / block break / explosion (`rumble.rs`, JNI). New **Controls > Controller** tab (buttons page + tuning page), saved as `pad_*` in `options.txt`. Button hints (2026-11-02): a bottom-right list of what the bound buttons do while a pad is in use (`Pad::hints`), drawn with the Controller Tooltip Selector pack's Xbox, PlayStation or Switch pictures (`assets/padbtn.rgba`, `tools/gen_pad_buttons.py`, the HUD texture's `PAD_Y` block) or as text; **Button Hints** and **Button Icons** in Controls > Controller tuning, saved as `pad_hints`, `pad_iconStyle`. New **Drop** bind (D-Down by default, `pad_drop`): throws one item of the selected slot. Written without a toolchain, not compiled. Not ported: gyro, DualSense extras, on-screen keyboard, chat / drop / perspective (not in mc-rs / b1.7.3); sprint is the row below, on L3. |
 | ImmediatelyFast ideas | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+7 tests, 1 extended) | `render/hud.rs`: the HUD text is one textured quad per glyph from a font atlas at the end of the HUD texture (was a quad per run of lit pixels: about 7x fewer text vertices); `render/items.rs`: `SignCache` keeps a sign's text quads between frames (5 s expiry); `gpuErrorTrace:true` in `options.txt` logs a backtrace with each wgpu error (`gpu/context.rs`). The rest of ImmediatelyFast (batching, map and animated-item atlases, framebuffer switching, Apple GL upload, resource pack handling) has no counterpart in mc-rs. Idea source: ImmediatelyFast 26.3, RaphiMC, LGPL-3.0. See the performance changelog. |
 | FerriteCore ideas | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+2 tests) | Lazy `Nibbles` (no array while all metadata is 0), flat `lod::Cols` for a real chunk's columns (no `Vec` per column; `Tile0::put` no longer clones 4096), exact-size LoD vectors. The rest of FerriteCore (blockstate / model / component dedupe, thread detector) has no counterpart in mc-rs. Idea source: FerriteCore, malte0811, MIT. See ROADMAP changelog. |
 | Lazy noise (C2ME idea 5) | written without a toolchain: not compiled; the generator tests incl. the golden `matches_java_reference` pass in a Linux scratch crate | The unread samples of the two big density stacks are not computed (`OctaveNoise::generate_masked_into`, masked per cached column); bit for bit the same terrain. See ROADMAP changelog. |
