 | Satchel restyle (2026-10-26) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+4 tests in `satchel.rs`); `tools/gen_satchel_ui.py` ran | The satchel and the recipe book in a grey GUI-pack look: stone panel with a red seam and corner marks, vanilla slots that touch, a brown book with a red-stitched spine, parchment pages in a brown frame. Text is flat (no shadow), whole-pixel sized and fitted to its box; the crafting grid is sized by the page's width as well as the height so the result never leaves the page; the category rim shows only under a finger. **NOT b1.7.3.** See the gameplay changelog. |
 | Map item (2026-10-30) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+8 tests in `world/map.rs`, +1 in `craft.rs`, `hud.rs` sheet test extended) | `world/map.rs` + `world/mapcolors.rs` (generated from the real classes by `tools/gen_mapcolors.py`): `ItemMap` 358, `MapData` (128 x 128 colour bytes, centre, scale, dimension), `MapStorage` (`<world>/data/map_<id>`, `idcounts`; ids from 0), `MapCoord` (the player's arrow, spinning in the Nether), `ItemMap.func_28011_a` ported line by line (16 interleaved strips a tick, shade by slope, water by depth, glass looked through, Nether hash) and `MapItemRenderer`'s colour decode. Recipe 358 = 8 paper round a compass in `craft::recipes()`; `ItemMap.onCreated` (new id, centred on the player, scale 3) runs on the next tick (`map::fresh` / `App::settle_maps`). The map in hand is a HUD sheet (`HudPipeline::push_map`, `assets/mapui.rgba` from `tools/gen_mapui.py`, `Backend::upload_map` in both renderers). Differences: only loaded chunks are read (the Java generates the 1024-block square), a flat sheet instead of the 3D two-handed model, no `map_N` label, no anaglyph grey. See the gameplay changelog. |
