+## QoL without a new meter (written 2026-11-01, NOT b1.7.3, Immersive Pack worlds only)
+
+Read from the design as a graph: every pressure has an answer (heat and cold: armor, torch, meal; wounds: hearth, bandage, bed, food), and three gaps are left, which are all about *information and recovery*, not about difficulty: pressures that cannot be seen, a death with no road back, and instruments that read only part of the world (the compass: place of the spawn; the clock: the hour; the map: the loaded chunks). Each line below closes one gap and adds **no meter, no hunger and no new block id** (owner's decision of 2026-11-01 stands). **Built 2026-11-01 (gameplay changelog (42)), all four, UNVERIFIED: not compiled, not run.** What differs from the lines below: Gauges has no options toggle (ponytail; add one only if the marks crowd a phone); the Almanac line is a coloured line under the clock's name in the hotbar flash and in the inventory tooltip (`combat::tooltip::lines`), and the flash stays up while a clock is held; the Death pile's pile is marked by a bit in the saved `age` of its items (no new field in the level file), its marker is a red cross that `HudPipeline::push_map` draws (no cell of `mapicons.png`), and a pile outside the map is drawn on the edge in its direction; the book pulls from the chests on a tap of a recipe only (a long press on the result still crafts from the bag). All four are gated by the pack (`rules::on()`), as the combat and the healing are (rule 5): with it OFF b1.7.3 plays as before, so no new switch. Every number is UNVERIFIED by play, and nothing here was compiled or run. Proposed order, easiest first: 1, 2, 3, 4.
+
+- **Gauges:** needs the state the code already holds (`biomelife::air`'s `hot` and `cold`, `Mend::bandaged`, the hearth's test in `App::heat_at_hand`, `Stamina`) -> the stamina bar takes a warm tint while `hot` and a cool one while `cold` is above 0, and one small mark shows beside the hearts while a bandage works or the hearth is ticking; nothing is stored, nothing is spent; Hooks: HUD (`render/hud`), `biomelife`, `combat::mend`, `stamina`; Overlaps: none (the hearts and the bar keep their meaning; this only reads them). Knob: the marks are options-menu toggles if they crowd a phone screen. Also closes the "no HUD mark" gap of `combat.md` C4. Inspiration: "status effect HUD", "temperature indicator".
+- **Almanac:** needs the day count (`world_ticks`, `season`) -> holding a clock shows the day number, the season and the minutes to dusk in the item tooltip line (the one a held stack already has); Hooks: clock (`render/anim`, the tooltip), `biomelife::season`, `sky`; Overlaps: clock (it told the hour only; now it also reads the calendar, so it is no more pointless than before, rule 2). Knob: the line shows only in a world where `biomeRules` is on, because the seasons exist only there. Inspiration: "seasons almanac", "calendar clock".
+- **Death pile:** needs a death (`Vitals`, the drop of the inventory, the existing source) -> the drop stays as one pile whose items last 4 times longer (`age < 24000` instead of `6000`) and a marker is drawn on any map the player carries (`map::Marker`, `MapData::markers`); the marker goes when the pile is picked up or gone; Hooks: death and respawn (`vitals`, `App::respawn_pos`), item lifetime (`items`), the map (`world::map`), the world save (`save`, the pile's age and the marker's place); Overlaps: map (it draws only the player now; this gives it a job a compass cannot do), compass (unchanged: spawn only). Loop (rule 3): nothing is made from nothing, the same items the player lost come back, and a pile still ends in the void, lava or the clock. Known limits: a death in lava or the void leaves nothing to find; `Drops::tick` steps every item whatever its distance, so a pile far from the player ages in real time (the chunk is not needed), which is the lifetime the line promises, but whether such an item rests where it fell in an unloaded chunk is not checked; `MAX_ITEMS` (256) still drops the oldest item first. Inspiration: "death waypoint", "corpse run", "gravestone".
+- **Craft from a nearby chest:** needs chests within 3 blocks of a workbench (`chest`, the existing container) -> the recipe book counts what those chests hold in `craftable` and `missing`, and a tap on a recipe takes the missing part from them; Hooks: `chest`, `book` (`craftable`, `missing`, `fill`), `craft` (the workbench); Overlaps: the satchel and the chests (rule 2: the bag keeps its limit and the chest keeps its job as the place things wait; the 3 block rule gives the workbench a new use and means a chest far away still has to be walked to). Knob: if the bag's limit stops being a pressure in play, shrink the radius or count one chest only. Inspiration: "craft from nearby chests", "refined storage lite".
+
+Ideas considered and not chosen: a thirst or a temperature meter (a hunger by another name, against the owner's decision); a gravestone block (one hook, and a new block id); a thermometer item (Gauges reads the same state with no item).
+
 ## Cortés Combat (written 2026-10-30, NOT b1.7.3)
 
 - **Combat rework (cone reach, cooldown, charge, guard, five weapon families; healing is "Healing without hunger" above):** needs wood, cobblestone, iron, diamond, gold, sticks, flint and iron blocks (existing sources) -> weapons that kill mobs; Hooks: crafting (`craft::recipes`, recipe book), durability (`craft::max_damage`), mobs and their damage window (`mobs`), stamina (`vitals`, guard), the touch HUD (`input/touch_ui`), sound (`audio`); Overlaps: sword, axe, hoe (they get a profile of the same system, so each keeps a job: the sword is the wide cheap cone with no special, the hoe sweeps). Switch: `combatRules`, default off. Plan: [`combat.md`](combat.md).
